Important finding: There is NO `HttpStatus.CONFLICT` / 409 handling anywhere in the codebase, and no custom "duplicate"/conflict exception. `@ResponseStatus` and `ResponseStatusException` are not used. The only place returning non-2xx from the controller directly is `HttpStatus.NOT_FOUND`. So 409 for duplicate telephone is currently unimplemented.

### 7. Tests for owner creation
There are NO dedicated unit/controller tests for `OwnerRestControllerV1`, `TelephoneNormalizer`, or `OwnerFieldsValidator`. The only owner-creation tests are black-box acceptance tests:

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AcceptanceTest.java` (lines 10-23):
```java
@Test void coreRejectsDuplicateTelephone() throws Exception {
    ObjectNode a = ownerNode();
    createOwnerOk(a);
    ObjectNode b = ownerNode();
    b.put("telephone", a.get("telephone").asText());
    createOwner(b).andExpect(status().isConflict());   // expects 409
}
@Test void functionalityAllowsDistinctTelephone() throws Exception {
    createOwnerOk(ownerNode());
    createOwner(ownerNode()).andExpect(status().is2xxSuccessful());
}
```
The class Javadoc states the rule: "telephone-unique: Reject creating an owner whose normalized telephone is already used by any other owner."

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AcceptanceBase.java` — the harness (`@SpringBootTest @AutoConfigureMockMvc @Transactional @WithMockUser(roles OWNER_ADMIN...)`). Key helpers: `createOwner`/`createOwnerOk` POST to `/api/owners`; `ownerNode()` builds a fully-unique valid owner; `uniqueTelephone()` returns `"04%08d"` (10-digit). `extractId` reads the `id` from the JSON body or the `Location` header.

### Summary of the gap
The acceptance test `coreRejectsDuplicateTelephone` expects a **409 Conflict** when creating an owner whose normalized telephone already belongs to another owner, but this rule is not implemented: `addOwner` normalizes the phone and saves without any uniqueness check, `OwnerRepository` has no `findByTelephone`, `ClinicServiceImpl.saveOwner` does no checking, and `ExceptionControllerAdvice` has no 409/conflict handler or corresponding exception. The DB `DataIntegrityViolationException` path maps to 404, not 409. Implementing the rule would touch: a repository lookup (or unique constraint), a service/controller check, a new conflict exception, and a 409 handler in the advice.

